# Hostile audit — attachment-cell diameter-square budget

**Date:** 2026-09-13
**Reviewed:** `target_c_attachment_cell_diameter_square_budget_2026-09-13.md`
**Disposition:** **PASS at stated proof-only full-core scope.**
**LEVEL I STATUS:** **STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.**

## 1. Area localization

The source scope is the no-container full-core branch. The audited harmonic-face
fidelity identifies all but `o(D^2)` of the full strict-rhombus area with local cell
faces. Every such rhombus is contained in its attachment polygon, and the attachment
polygon interiors are pairwise disjoint. Hence the sum of cell areas is at least
`A_4-o(D^2)`, with no claim that the cells cover the force hull.

The full-core near-disk theorem supplies

`A_4=(pi/4-o(1))D^2`.

This is not valid for an arbitrary selected carrier, and the reviewed note keeps that
scope explicit.

**Verdict:** PASS.

## 2. Isodiametric step

For each convex attachment polygon, `area(P_r)<=pi d_r^2/4`. Summing gives

`sum d_r^2 >= (4/pi) sum area(P_r) >= D^2-o(D^2)`.

The inequality `sum d_r >= sqrt(sum d_r^2)` is valid because the diameters are
nonnegative. Thus (CSB.1)--(CSB.2) have the stated constants.

**Verdict:** PASS.

## 3. Five-currency substitution

The exact finite ledger is

`2(q-k)+2=sum d_r+G_D+Q+u_B+k`.

Inserting `sum d_r>=D-o(D)` gives

`G_D+Q+u_B+k<=2(q-k)-D+o(D)`.

The Type-II identity `e_BB=Q+2k+u_B` gives `Q+u_B+k=e_BB-k`, so the second form is
also exact at finite scale up to the displayed `o(D)` area loss.

**Verdict:** PASS.

## 4. Limits and non-implications

The audit does not promote the result to theorem-state authority. The budget is an
upper bound on a combined currency and does not control any one term. It does not
close the high-detour full-core branch, the inactive-container branch, or the Level-I
quantifier. Contact-isolated source points remain outside the core cell ledger.

**Final verdict:** PASS at proof-only scope; theorem state and C-II status remain
unchanged.
